eliberately NOT modified — its documented local-vs-jira contract stays intact for callers that honour it'","Consumers of compute_mutations outside a new planner file: src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py:237 (production), src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py (drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions), plus ~15 test modules","Plan 'Out of scope' lists 'shadow cutover', implying existing callers are NOT rewired in this task"],"finding":"Step 3 ('Refactor existing differ decisions into plan mutation values') does not name the target module/file for the new planner and value types, nor state whether the existing differ.py / mutation.py are edited in place; 'Refactor' is ambiguous. differ.compute_mutations has out-of-dir/production consumers (run_differs.py, reconcile_helpers.drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions) and a large test suite that would require updating if it is modified in place — which would contradict the out-of-scope 'shadow cutover'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc5b1607a1a4b57b5","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 / 'Out of scope' section","norm_id":"nc5a701fe15612e22","priority":0.0754,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer/implementer cannot tell whether the new planner is a new module leaving differ.py intact, or an in-place rewrite that breaks run_differs.py and the differ test suite"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severi